+- **No idle between steps (experiment; product owner entry of 2026-11-08, card 361 retro).** While this entry is on trial: every background wait has an armed monitor whose condition matches success, failure and expiry (a success-only line, which a crashed launcher can never produce, is not a monitor); a launcher's first output is read within 60 seconds of its launch; a wrapper script writes an end flag in a trap; and a turn ends only at a card or cycle boundary after the next step has been launched or a monitor is armed on the wait that blocks it (the next Ready draft after a close, the gate review after a green push, the sign-off after the review, the retro after the sign-off, the close-out after CI). Every retro reports idle minutes per card (minutes with nothing running and nothing landing) and Dispatch nudges per card, with the cause of each.
+  - Hypothesis: an armed, failure-aware monitor on every wait and a next step launched in the same turn leave no idle gap for a nudge to fill. Metric: idle minutes per card (card 203: about 30, the retro-voices launcher died on a syntax error and its monitor could only expire; card 361: about 0) and Dispatch nudges per card (card 203: 1; the product owner counted six cases on cards 178 to 203), target 0 each. Counter-metric: a next step started too early and relaunched (card 186: a gate review on a pre-revision tip, about 25 minutes). Trial: the next 3 cards, counted from Decider D230. Owner: the facilitator.
